cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or results obtained with it, please cite the paper
  given under "preferred-citation". When referring to the code itself,
  please additionally cite the archived version of this repository.
type: software
title: >-
  Code for "Splitting-strategies for arbitrary-order fully mixed finite
  element discretizations of the Biot equations"
authors:
  - family-names: Dağlı
    given-names: Tugay
    affiliation: TU Chemnitz
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
# repository-code: "https://github.com/<github-user>/splitting_4_arbitrary_mfem_biot"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
keywords:
  - Biot equations
  - poroelasticity
  - mixed finite elements
  - weak symmetry
  - fixed-stress splitting
  - NGSolve
abstract: >-
  Scripts and result files reproducing all numerical experiments of the paper
  (Figures 1, 3, 4 and Tables 1-2, 4-8): a five-field, weakly symmetric fully
  mixed finite element discretization of the Biot equations of arbitrary
  order, solved with the fixed-stress splitting with destabilization.
